  "environment_caveats": [
    "First audit on the apex. apex_cutover.completed_at is 2026-09-19T00:24:09+00:00, so https://dissrestoration.com was audited. It serves the Rank AI build (server: cloudflare, HTTP 200 on all 6 URLs, no x-robots-tag). SEO counts toward the verdict this run.",
    "The prior audit (2026-08-26) ran on the Cloudflare Pages staging preview. Deltas are matched by path across origins. The +31 SEO delta on every page is the staging noindex artifact going away, not an on-page change. Performance and LCP deltas mix a real code change (new gtag script) with a different edge/CDN path and single-run Lighthouse variance.",
    "Lighthouse ran DESKTOP only (for_mobile=false). Mobile scores would typically run 10-20 performance points lower, and the 1.36 MB logo.png would hurt far more on mobile.",
    "lighthouse_issues is capped at the 5 highest-impact failing audits per URL. render-blocking-insight (single 9 KB CSS, ~50 ms), cache-insight (Cloudflare email-decode.min.js, 0 KiB savings), network-dependency-tree-insight and forced-reflow-insight (fire page only) also fail but fall outside the cap.",
    "has_micromarkup_errors fires on the 5 pages that ship FAQPage JSON-LD. Question objects carry name + acceptedAnswer but no answerCount/text. Those are QAPage fields that Google's FAQPage rich result does not require, so this is scored low rather than as a schema defect.",
    "Two service-landing slots were filled from a three-way priority tie at 9.0 (water-damage-restoration, fire-damage-restoration, mold-remediation). Kept the same two as last month for comparability. No service-area has primary: true and the business city (Farrell, PA) has no area page, so warren-oh was used per the fallback rule."
  ],
